# Latest Golden versions

When the user says **latest golden** or **WEBSITE LATEST GOLDEN**, restore the **22 October 2026 website**. Extension and admin stay on 19 September 2026 until the user names a newer one for those.

| Name | Git tag | What it freezes |
|---|---|---|
| **WEBSITE LATEST GOLDEN VERSION** | `golden-website-2026-10-22` | wrrapd.com after the header/footer wordmark restore |
| **EXTENSION LATEST GOLDEN VERSION** | `golden-extension-2026-09-19` | Chrome extension **3.0.10** |
| **ADMIN LATEST GOLDEN VERSION** | `golden-admin-2026-09-19` | Tracking Command Center (`tracking-platform/`) |

Website inventory: [GOLDEN-VERSIONS-2026-10-22.md](../../GOLDEN-VERSIONS-2026-10-22.md)

September website tag `golden-website-2026-09-19` and homepage tag `golden-homepage-2026-09-08` are historical.

Social images are copy-paste banners. Never rewrite the live header or footer. See [wrrapd-social-banners-only.mdc](./wrrapd-social-banners-only.mdc).

## Restore (GCP VM — never `git pull`)

```bash
cd /home/phill/wrrapd-GCP
git fetch origin --tags
# Website (October 2026):
git checkout golden-website-2026-10-22 -- wordpress/ docs/SOCIAL-SHARE-CARDS.md docs/WORDPRESS-SITE-EDITS-LOG.md .cursor/rules/wrrapd-social-banners-only.mdc .cursor/rules/wrrapd-latest-golden-versions.mdc GOLDEN-VERSIONS-2026-10-22.md
# Extension:
git checkout golden-extension-2026-09-19 -- extension/
# Admin / Command Center:
git checkout golden-admin-2026-09-19 -- tracking-platform/
```

Then: SiteGround gets changed MU copies + cache flush; Windows rebuilds the extension only if `extension/` was restored; Cloud Run only if tracking files changed.
